WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:00.667
We.

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.768
We're back from St John's,

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.068
the site

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:02.869
where the Titans started

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.004
its ill fated journey

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.972
as the investigation picks up here.

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.007
A search for answers

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:07.474
is happening

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.541
for another deadly sea

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.010
disaster, this one in the Mediterranean

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.211
and where more than 700

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.079
migrants were crammed on a boat

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.114
that sank last week off

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.315
the coast of Greece.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.216
And the testimonies

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:16.983
from survivors

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:19.019
depict chaos and desperation.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.120
An investigation

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.087
by CNN's Jomana

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.523
Karadsheh raises some questions

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.291
about the statements from Greek officials

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.761
about what actually led to this tragedy.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.064
The desperate,

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.232
exhausting week

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.367
for the promise of a new life in Europe.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:35.902
These Pakistanis

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:38.038
crammed into a small room by smugglers

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:38.972
in Libya.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.407
Some of them believed to be among

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.208
the hundreds presumed dead.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.243
These last images

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.277
before they embarked

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.212
on their Ill-Fated journey.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.314
About 750 refugees

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.949
and migrants were packed into this

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.818
fishing vessel bound for Italy

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.319
before it capsized off the

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.220
coast of Greece.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.757
Only 104 survived.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:58.224
And with

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:58.425
them,

00:00:58.425 --> 00:00:59.993
the harrowing accounts of what

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.362
they'd been through for them all along.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:03.897
I can still hear the voice of a woman

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.432
calling out for help.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.299
You would swim

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.500
and move the floating bodies

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.635
out of your way.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.836
The Syrian survivor

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:11.071
spoke to us from Greece.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.439
He asked for his identity

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:14.474
to be concealed for security reasons.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:15.842
His and other accounts

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:16.810
obtained by CNN

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.044
not only contradict

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.113
the official Greek version of events,

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.181
but point to fault

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.683
on the part of the Greek Coast Guard.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.418
Greek authorities who watched

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.853
and were communication with the boat

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:29.155
for an entire day in insist

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.857
that it was not in distress

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.592
and refused assistance.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.827
Our investigation

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:37.197
tells a very different story

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.399
Just before one p.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:40.567
M on June 13th,

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.602
the boat was first spotted by the U.S.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.804
Border Patrol agency Frontex,

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:45.572
which says it

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.006
notified Greek authorities

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:47.941
of a, quote, heavily

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.476
overcrowded fishing vessel.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.479
Those on board were in distress,

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:53.379
lost at sea

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.348
with no food or water for days,

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.250
according to survivors and activists.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.218
In touch with the boat

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:59.886
throughout the day.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.955
At about 7 p.m., an activist

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.056
in Italy recorded

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:03.756
one of the calls,

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.159
capturing the horror on board.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:06.826
I'm going.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:07.694
I'm going to happen.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.896
That was going to happen

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:13.833
as activists

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:16.069
repeatedly relayed calls for a rescue

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.137
to authorities

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:17.737
to merchant

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.305
vessels, approached the boats

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.007
instructed by the Greek Coast Guard

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.076
to provide the boat with food and water.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:26.312
But as darkness fell at 10:40 p.m.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.381
a Greek Coast Guard vessel moves in.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.517
Now the only ship on the scene

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.684
3 hours later,

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.186
the haunting last words

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.521
from the boat to the activist

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:35.889
group alarmed phone.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.056
Hello, my friend.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:40.393
The ship you send is the line cuts out.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:41.561
What happened

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.830
next is likely to raise more questions

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.032
as the investigations continue.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:46.666
Survivors

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.701
tell us it was a botched attempt

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:49.736
by the Greek Coast Guard

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:50.570
to tow their boat

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.772
that caused it to capsize

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.141
and they decided to throw as a rope.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.377
So the guys at the front tied it.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.478
They told us

00:02:58.478 --> 00:02:59.746
the boat tilted to the right

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.381
and everyone was screaming.

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:03.383
People began falling into the sea

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.817
and the boat capsized.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:05.385
People couldn't

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:06.920
get out from under the boat.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.921
The Greek Coast Guard

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.155
have declined our request

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:09.956
for an interview,

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.357
but in previous comments,

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.426
they've denied towing the trawler, saying

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.894
when the boat capsized,

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.696
we were not even next to it.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.264
How could we be towing it?

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.466
Instead, they blamed a shift in weight,

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.035
probably caused by panic

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:26.206
For years, Greek authorities

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.874
have been accused of systematically

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:28.675
and violently

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:32.145
pushing back migrants and refugees.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:33.513
Video like this one released

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.547
by the Turkish government

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:35.315
captured the now

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:36.883
well documented practice.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.685
Greece denies

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.254
this deadly incident is not just about

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.655
what they may have done.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:45.024
It's also about what they didn't do.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.627
It was clear it was unseaworthy.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:49.028
It was clear that it is

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.397
part of the offshore trafficking movement

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.733
from Libya to Europe.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.868
So the authorities had a responsibility

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.470
to intervene, to save life.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.204
As Fortress

00:03:58.204 --> 00:03:59.038
Europe hardens

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.840
its immigration policies to deter

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.675
some of the world's most vulnerable.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.744
This disaster will almost certainly

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:07.013
not be the last

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.650
And, Anderson, as you heard there, Greek

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.684
authorities are telling us

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:12.518
that they're continuing

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:14.621
to investigate this incident.

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:15.521
But the Greek Coast

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.257
Guard, Greek authorities in the past over

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.024
the past few years

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:18.758
have been

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:21.027
accused of violently pushing back

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.328
migrants and refugees.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.430
And we've never really seen any results

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.665
of investigations in the past.

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:26.733
So the question right now

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.134
is whether there should be any sort

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:29.035
of an international

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:31.070
independent investigation. Anderson,

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.174
yeah, this has been going on and on.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.409
Jomana Karadsheh, I appreciate it.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:36.776
Thank you.

